            <ArticleTitle>Successful treatment of a ruptured mycotic coronary artery aneurysm.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1780-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Documented mycotic aneurysms of the coronary arteries are unusual, and antemortem identification of such an aneurysm is rare. We present the case of a patient who had successful management of a ruptured mycotic aneurysm of a coronary artery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
